As before, we figure out the areas labeled in the diagram. Then, we note that <cmath>\dfrac{EF}{AE} = \dfrac{x}{60} = \dfrac{120-x}{180}</cmath>
Even simpler:  <cmath>\dfrac{EF}{AE} = \dfrac{x}{60} = \dfrac{120}{240}</cmath>
Solving gives <imath>x = \boxed{\textbf{(B) }30}</imath>. 
